{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_cluster", "label": "Cluster", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A group of ActorSystems that gossip membership, detect failures and route messages, so the same code that worked single-node still works with refs pointing at any node.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_clusterbootstrap", "label": "Cluster.bootstrap", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Packages system creation, seed resolution, join and SIGTERM/SIGINT wiring into one call; discovery defaults to an env-driven chain and local dev with no env produces a single-node cluster.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_clusterjoin", "label": "Cluster.join", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Resolves once this node has finished joining, but peers' views converge over the next few gossip rounds, so startup logic that needs every peer to know about this node should act in a SelfUp handler.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_clusteroptions", "label": "ClusterOptions", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "host+port is the address peers dial, seeds is the bootstrap hint (empty = 'I am the first'), roles tag the node for routers and shard regions to filter on.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_membership_states", "label": "Membership state machine", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "joining, weakly-up, up, unreachable, leaving, exiting, removed; a removed member is kept as a tombstone for a TTL (default 24 h) so stale gossip from a slow peer cannot resurrect it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_gossip", "label": "Gossip membership protocol", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Each member exchanges its view with a random reachable peer every gossipIntervalMs and merges by picking the higher version per member, so every concurrent update converges without a central coordinator.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_leader", "label": "Leader is the lowest-addressed up member", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Emphatically not the oldest member: the one property a leader must have is that every node names the same one, and address order gives that from gossip every node already has, with no monotonic join sequence on the wire. The cost is that leadership is stable across a pod restart but not across a re-address.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_subscription_replay", "label": "Subscription replay (events / snapshot)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "subscribe replays the membership that already exists so a late listener still learns the world it joined; 'snapshot' answers where things stand in one callback and marks where the replay ends, which the event form cannot.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_currentclusterstate", "label": "CurrentClusterState", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Never published on the event stream: it describes one subscriber's starting point, not something that happened to the cluster; unreachable is a subset of members, not a set beside it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_single_node_mode", "label": "Single-node cluster mode", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A cluster of one is valid - the local node auto-promotes to leader and every extension works as in a larger cluster, so cluster code can be developed without a Docker Compose setup.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_system_cluster_option", "label": "system.cluster stays an Option", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A cluster binds a transport and starts gossip, heartbeat and failure-detection timers, so it is never created on demand the way a lazily-initialised extension would be - a local-only system must not grow a cluster because something asked for it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_cluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_clusterjoin", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_cluster", "target": 